================================================================================
TEST 20358 -- Loopback between two ports on same switch
================================================================================
Run:      2026-10-13 11:25:18-11:27:47 NZDT (tb470 clock; the x230 clock reads NZ wall time
          labelled "UTC", ~9 s behind tb470: device log "no shutdown" 11:26:42 vs tb470 11:26:51)
Bench:    tb470, console u0; Test Engineer terrenceb@terrenceb-dl
Tester:   bench-runner (by hand: tools/tb ckcon (tools/ckcon.py, incl. its @poll gate), tools/linerate.py,
          tools/rc2cfg.py; no framework script)
Graded:   tester
Case:     AWPTCM-T20358 (/xSTP/RSTP), objective "When a switch port receives its own BPDU from the same
          edge port, it sets the port to the blocking state. When it no longer receives BPDUs, it sets the
          port to the forwarding state.", 1 step
Build:    swi_f awplus_main-20261008-57 (x230v2_28GS-awplus_main-20261008-57.rel, build date
          Thu Oct 8 00:10:09 UTC 2026), bootloader 6.2.40
Configs:  swi_f.cfg (running-config after setup, before the loop is closed: port1.0.7 is still `shutdown`
          there, its `no shutdown` is quoted in STEP 1; saved to startup: no)

VERDICT: PASS -- port1.0.7, receiving its own bridge's RSTP BPDUs over the loop lead, is Backup/Discarding and
         transmits none of 8356 broadcast frames
      loop closed (port1.0.6 <-> port1.0.7) ..... both ports up, VLAN 105, RSTP on
      Port11 = port1.0.7 role / state ........... PASS  (Backup / Discarding 5.1 s after no shutdown; Received RSTP,
                                                         Designated Bridge = own bridge, Designated Port Id 838e)
      broadcast from "IXIA" (tb470 eth3) ......... 8356 x 1500-byte frames at 10 Mb/s into port1.0.5
      backup port transmits nothing .............. PASS  (port1.0.7 output broadcast +0; port1.0.6 broadcast +8356;
                                                         nothing returned to eth3: port1.0.5 output broadcast +0)
      state after the traffic .................... unchanged (Backup / Discarding, forward-transitions 1)
CAVEAT:  The "hub/switch" of the case is a direct copper lead between two ports of the DUT, so the loop is the
         x230 seeing its own BPDUs; the "IXIA" is tb470 eth3 sending with tools/linerate.py at 10 Mb/s. This
         build words the role "Backup"; the case's "(Loopback Disabled)" is not printed. The objective's
         second sentence (back to forwarding when BPDUs stop) is not a step of the case and was not exercised:
         on a direct lead, stopping port1.0.6's BPDUs means taking the link down or filtering BPDUs, which
         would open a real loop. port1.0.7 sent one multicast frame (not broadcast) in the counter window.

