  => STEP 1 PASS: with the loop closed, port1.0.7 (Port11) is Backup / Discarding because it receives its own
     bridge's RSTP BPDUs from port1.0.6. Under 8356 broadcast frames from eth3, the designated end
     port1.0.6 flooded all 8356 onto the lead and port1.0.7 received them, but port1.0.7 transmitted 0
     broadcast packets (its only output was 1 multicast frame, matched by port1.0.6's input multicast +1),
     nothing came back to eth3 (port1.0.5 output broadcast 0, eth3 saw only its own frames), and port1.0.7
     stayed Backup / Discarding with no forward transition: the backup port forwarded no packet.
